body:
`progressive-chat-ui-pull-requests` exists to be carried here once its work is tried and accepted; this is that carry. In from its fifteen commits since `b99215f`:

- **the no-auto-size answer, whole**: their `2389d73` / `cef69fe` / `9215f7c` series is the same fix `cc59d79` gave main, arrived at independently -- four conflicts in `settings`, `drawer`, `controls`, `message_list` resolved to the ui-repo's side, because this carry puts that repo at the foundation. What goes with it: main's `words_wide` machinery and the one-word fix inside it (`98c4c39`) leave with the machinery they served -- the texts keep their measured size directly, the way `skiff-widgets` carries its own;
- **the panel of conversations** redesigned (`cae7c07`): a heading, a search of its own, Tasks and Remote as one ground in two, a new chat, the settings at the foot of the rows -- with the rows kept to one line and cut with an ellipsis (`1fa2282`, `9ef1c18`), and what the settings page says of itself (`7fb2684`);
- **the press that asks for one test notification** (`8fc9caa`) with its plumbing -- `src/platform/notified*`, the Android side, `requests` and `screens`;
- **`shoot.yml`** -- a hand-asked workflow that shoots the window at a chosen screen, because a corner's roundness is not a thing a check can say;
- their updated `probe_settings` and readouts (`f302b1c`, `c4ee2b5`).

What stays from main untouched: the anthropic wave, the notes (with the added paragraph), the fold probe, the clipboard read-back, the face kept every frame in `program.cc`.

**One deliberate subtraction** (`9da39a4`): the staging's live green readouts -- the column's numbers over the messages, the list's at its foot, the settings' overlap sayings -- came along with it, and they print on every frame of a page meant for people. Main had removed its own diagnostics the same way (`ada774b`); the carry takes the ui without them, and putting any of them back is one revert away.

Verified on this tree by hand: the fold answers a press on its words and shuts again, the Info chip's line of tokens stands up and goes, a room's row changes the room and the first room's row changes it back (this last one failed until the readouts came out -- they kept the mirror from ever matching itself), no page errors; screenshots show the carried panel with nothing green on it. CI: check, web and desktop green on `9da39a45`, android in hand; asked by hand because pull_request runs have not been starting on these branches today.

**Two further waves of main were folded in along the way** (the branch keeps pace with main): their **seven switches** across Multimodal, Network and Memory & Data and the **test-notification press** were integrated with the carried panel — nine groups, both features live, and the page itself says so in the mirror (`Notifications`, `Send a test notification`, every group name read back true on a build of this tree); and the fold's new **tool calls** (`8ae778e`) were kept — sized the way the rest of the fold is sized, by what measures the words, so `words_wide`, `line_tall` and `how_it_stands` leave with the machinery they belonged to (a text must never ask for `autoSize`, and must not need a hand-measured width either). One line of their own was picked up on the way: `f(fTest)` was missing from `forEachChild` in the staging drawer, leaving the Test row undrawn — added with the rest.

Verification of the final tree (`fd809a59`): check, web, desktop and android all green; a hand-run probe reads the fold open with `conversation_search: …` lines behind it, the Info chip's tokens line up and away, the room changed and changed back — all true, no page errors; the settings page reads all nine groups.
